T Six-axis K'NEX arm on a Caterpillar lever stand: rigid linkage only, no strings or bands
# U = 37.5 mm, z up, desk at z = 0. Nothing in the drive path can pull only: every axis is driven
# by rods, cranks and gears, so every lever pushes AND pulls its axis.
! ground frame: a 4U square deck on four anchored feet, with the yaw axle standing in the middle
C P1 B7 2,2,1.5 z -x
C P1v B7 2,2,1.5 x -z
C P2 B7 2,-2,1.5 z y
C P2v B7 2,-2,1.5 x -z
C P3 B7 -2,-2,1.5 z x
C P3v B7 -2,-2,1.5 x -z
C P4 B7 -2,2,1.5 z -y
C P4v B7 -2,2,1.5 x -z
C M1 W8 0,2,1.5
C M2 W8 2,0,1.5
C M3 W8 0,-2,1.5
C M4 W8 -2,0,1.5
C BC B7 0,0,1.5 z x+y
C BCV B7 0,0,1.5 y z
R P1 M1
R M1 P4
R P4 M4
R M4 P3
R P3 M3
R M3 P2
R P2 M2
R M2 P1
R BC P1
R BC P2
R BC P3
R BC P4
! feet: the only parts that touch the desk, and the four points the stand is clamped by
C FT1 W8 2,2,0.5 x y
C FT2 W8 2,-2,0.5 x y
C FT3 W8 -2,-2,0.5 x y
C FT4 W8 -2,2,0.5 x y
R FT1 P1v
R FT2 P2v
R FT3 P3v
R FT4 P4v
A FT1
A FT2
A FT3
A FT4
W ballast M4 mass=600
! the yaw axle stands on the centre 3D pair and is capped: the house turns on it
R BCV 0,0,5.5 red
C YCAP D1 0,0,5.5 y -z
! the house: a braced box on two spacer-parked hubs. Its -x face is left open on purpose: the swing
! pinion runs down it and the operator's console hangs off it.
H Y1 W8 0,0,2.5
H Y2 W8 0,0,4.5
P 0,0,2.3 silver
P 0,0,2.7 silver
C CA B7 1,1,2.5 z -x
C Av B7 1,1,2.5 -y z
C CB B7 1,-1,2.5 z y
C Bv B7 1,-1,2.5 -x z
C CC B7 -1,-1,2.5 z x
C Cv B7 -1,-1,2.5 y z
C CD B7 -1,1,2.5 z -y
C Dv B7 -1,1,2.5 y z
C PN W8 -1,0,2.5
R Y1 CA
R Y1 CB
R Y1 CC
R Y1 CD
R CA CB
R CB CC
R CC PN
R PN CD
R CD CA
C CA2 B7 1,1,4.5 z -x
C A2v B7 1,1,4.5 -x -z
C CB2 B7 1,-1,4.5 z y
C B2v B7 1,-1,4.5 y -z
C CC2 B7 -1,-1,4.5 z x
C C2v B7 -1,-1,4.5 y -z
C CD2 B7 -1,1,4.5 z -y
C D2v B7 -1,1,4.5 y z
C PN2 W8 -1,0,4.5
R Y2 CA2
R Y2 CB2
R Y2 CC2
R Y2 CD2
R CA2 CB2
R CB2 CC2
R CC2 PN2
R PN2 CD2
R CD2 CA2
R Av A2v
R Bv B2v
R Cv C2v
R Dv D2v
R A2v Bv
R Cv B2v
R D2v Av
! CONSOLE: the operator's stand. It hangs off the open -x face of the house and is braced down to
! the lower ring, so every lever pushes against the machine and the machine pushes against the desk.
C KA0 W8 -3,-1,2.5 -y x
C KB0 W8 -3,1,2.5 -y x
R CC KA0
R CD KB0
R C2v KA0
R D2v KB0
C KA B7 -3,-1,4.5 z -y
C KAv B7 -3,-1,4.5 y -z
C KB B7 -3,1,4.5 z -y
C KBv B7 -3,1,4.5 y -z
R KA0 KAv
R KB0 KBv
R CC2 KA
R CD2 KB
R CC2 KB
C KC B7 -3,-2,4.5 x y
C KCv B7 -3,-2,4.5 y z
C KM W8 -3,0,4.5 x y
C KD B7 -3,2,4.5 x y
C KDv B7 -3,2,4.5 y z
R KC KA
R KA KM
R KM KB
R KB KD
C KE1 B7 -2,-2,4.5 z x
C KE1v B7 -2,-2,4.5 y z
C KE2 B7 -2,2,4.5 z x
C KE2v B7 -2,2,4.5 y z
