R KDv KE2
R KE1 KA
R KE2 KB
! the console mast, and the lever shaft one unit in front of it
C LT1 B7 -3,-2,6.5 x -z
C LT2 W8 -3,-1,6.5 z y
C LT3 W8 -3,0,6.5 x -z
C LT4 W8 -3,1,6.5 z y
C LT5 B7 -3,2,6.5 x -y
R KC LT1
R KD LT5
R LT1 LT2
R LT2 LT3
R LT3 LT4
R LT4 LT5
R KC LT3
R KM LT5
C LS1 B7 -2,-2,6.5 z x+y
C LS1v B7 -2,-2,6.5 y -z
C LS2 B7 -2,2,6.5 z -x
C LS2v B7 -2,2,6.5 y -z
R LT1 LS1
R LT5 LS2
R LT2 LS1
R LT4 LS2
R KE1v LS1v
R KE2v LS2v
R LS1 LS2
! AXIS 1 swing: a 14-tooth pinion on a vertical shaft in the house rolls round the 34-tooth gear on
! the yaw bearing. 14 + 34 teeth mesh at exactly 37.5 mm, one green rod, so the pinion shaft stands
! one unit from the axle. The tiller is tan-clipped to that shaft; without the clip it would spin
! inside its own hub and drive nothing.
R -1,0,1.5 -1,0,5.5 red
C PSB D1 -1,0,1.5 x z
C PST D1 -1,0,5.5 x -z
P -1,0,2.3 blue
P -1,0,2.7 blue
G ghouse Y1 teeth=34
G gpin PN teeth=14
H YLV W8 -1,0,5.2
L YLV
C YLG D1 -2.41421,0,5.2 z x
R YLV YLG
F YLG 0,0.01,0 swing
! the shoulder deck: a braced box on the house top ring carrying the shoulder shaft
R 1,-2,6.5 1,2,6.5 red
C SC1 D1 1,-2,6.5 z y
C SC2 D1 1,2,6.5 z -y
H N1 W8 1,-1,6.5 -z
H N2 W8 1,1,6.5 -z
R B2v N1
R A2v N2
R C2v N1
R D2v N2
! THE LEVER BANK: five bell cranks riding one red shaft on the console, handles up, crank pins
! forward. Every lever end is a hub parked between two spacers, so it is a true revolute: the run
! pushes as well as it pulls and no axis needs a return spring.
! lever 2 - shoulder
H LV2 W8 -2,0,6.5
P -2,-0.15,6.5 blue
P -2,0.15,6.5 blue
C LV2H D1 -2,0,10.5 y -z
R LV2 LV2H
C LV2C W8 0,0,8.5 x-z y
R LV2 LV2C
C LV2P D1 0,-1,8.5 z y
R LV2C LV2P
H LV2K W8 0,-0.5,8.5
P 0,-0.65,8.5 blue
P 0,-0.35,8.5 blue
! lever 3 - elbow
H LV3 W8 -2,-0.7,6.5
P -2,-0.85,6.5 blue
P -2,-0.55,6.5 blue
C LV3H D1 -2,-0.7,10.5 y -z
R LV3 LV3H
C LV3C W8 -1,-0.7,6.5 z -y
R LV3 LV3C
C LV3P D1 -1,-1.7,6.5 z y
R LV3C LV3P
H LV3K W8 -1,-1.2,6.5
P -1,-1.35,6.5 blue
P -1,-1.05,6.5 blue
! lever 4 - wristpitch
H LV4 W8 -2,0.7,6.5
P -2,0.55,6.5 blue
P -2,0.85,6.5 blue
C LV4H D1 -2,0.7,10.5 y -z
R LV4 LV4H
C LV4C W8 -1,0.7,6.5 z y
R LV4 LV4C
C LV4P D1 -1,1.7,6.5 z -y
R LV4C LV4P
H LV4K W8 -1,1.2,6.5
P -1,1.05,6.5 blue
P -1,1.35,6.5 blue
! lever 5 - roll
H LV5 W8 -2,-1.5,6.5
P -2,-1.65,6.5 blue
P -2,-1.35,6.5 blue
C LV5H D1 -2,-1.5,10.5 y -z
R LV5 LV5H
C LV5C W8 -1,-1.5,5.5 x+z -y
R LV5 LV5C
C LV5P D1 -1,-2.5,5.5 z y
R LV5C LV5P
H LV5K W8 -1,-2,5.5
P -1,-2.15,5.5 blue
P -1,-1.85,5.5 blue
! lever 6 - grip
H LV6 W8 -2,1.5,6.5
P -2,1.35,6.5 blue
P -2,1.65,6.5 blue
C LV6H D1 -2,1.5,10.5 y -z
R LV6 LV6H
C LV6C W8 0,1.5,4.5 x+z y
R LV6 LV6C
C LV6P D1 0,2.5,4.5 z -y
R LV6C LV6P
H LV6K W8 0,2.2,4.5
P 0,2.05,4.5 blue
P 0,2.35,4.5 blue
F LV2H 0.01,0,0 shoulder
F LV3H 0.01,0,0 elbow
F LV4H 0.01,0,0 wristpitch
F LV5H 0.01,0,0 roll
F LV6H 0.01,0,0 grip
! THE UPPER ARM: a flat triangle in the plane y=0, tan-clipped to the shoulder shaft so arm and
! shaft turn together. The four relay cranks ride free hubs on that same shaft: that is what lets a
! lever at the base reach past a joint without a cable.
H UA W8 1,0,6.5 z
L UA
C UM8 B7 1,0,8.5 -y -x-z
C UM8v B7 1,0,8.5 z -y
R UA UM8
R 3,-2,6.5 3,2,6.5 red
C EC1 D1 3,-2,6.5 z y
C EC2 D1 3,2,6.5 z -y
H EB W8 3,0,6.5 -z
R UA EB
R UM8 EB
P 1,-1.75,6.5 blue
P 1,-1.25,6.5 blue
P 1,-0.75,6.5 blue
P 1,-0.25,6.5 blue
P 1,0.25,6.5 blue
P 1,0.75,6.5 blue
P 1,1.25,6.5 blue
P 1,1.75,6.5 blue
! AXIS 2 shoulder drive: lever 2 -> green coupler -> the 2U mast on the upper arm. A four-bar, so
! pushing the lever forward lifts the arm and pulling it back drives the arm down. No spring anywhere.
C UP2 D1 1,-1,8.5 z y
R UM8 UP2
H UM8K W8 1,-0.5,8.5
P 1,-0.65,8.5 blue
P 1,-0.35,8.5 blue
R LV2K UM8K
! FOUR RELAY CRANKS on the shoulder shaft. Each is a bell crank riding a free hub on the shoulder
! axis: the console lever swings it, and its output crank drives a coupler running parallel to the
! upper arm. Crank, coupler and the arm make a parallelogram, so the link at the far end keeps the
! attitude the lever gave it however the shoulder moves. That is the whole trick of this machine.
! relay RS3 rides the shoulder axis
H RS3 W8 1,-0.5,6.5 -x+z
C RS3I W8 0,-0.5,7.5 x+z -y
C RS3IP D1 0,-1.5,7.5 z y
H RS3IK W8 0,-1.2,7.5
P 0,-1.35,7.5 blue
P 0,-1.05,7.5 blue
R RS3 RS3I
R RS3I RS3IP
R LV3K RS3IK
C RS3O W8 2,-0.5,7.5 x-z -y
C RS3OP D1 2,-1.5,7.5 z y
H RS3OK W8 2,-1,7.5
P 2,-1.15,7.5 blue
P 2,-0.85,7.5 blue
R RS3 RS3O
R RS3O RS3OP
! relay RS4 rides the shoulder axis
H RS4 W8 1,0.5,6.5 -x+z
C RS4I W8 0,0.5,7.5 x+z y
C RS4IP D1 0,1.5,7.5 z -y
H RS4IK W8 0,1.2,7.5
P 0,1.05,7.5 blue
P 0,1.35,7.5 blue
