! THE WRIST LINK, and the two relays that ride the wrist axis. From here the drive has to turn a
! corner: the runs from the base all rotate about y, the roll and the jaw rotate about x. A rod
! sliding vertically through a guide hub is what turns that corner - one slider per axis, driven in
! the xz plane by the relay and driving in the yz plane through a pin that lies along the roll axis.
H WL W8 5,0,6.5 x+z
L WL
C WT B7 6,0,7.5 -y x-z
C WTv B7 6,0,7.5 z y
C WD W8 7,0,6.5 y -x
C WS B7 7,0,7.5 -y -x
C WSv B7 7,0,7.5 z -y
R WL WT
R WL WD
R WT WD
R WT WS
R WD WS
C WTP D1 6,1,7.5 z -y
R WT WTP
H WTK W8 6,0.7,7.5
P 6,0.55,7.5 blue
P 6,0.85,7.5 blue
R RE4OK WTK
P 5,-1.35,6.5 blue
P 5,-0.65,6.5 blue
P 5,0.15,6.5 blue
P 5,1.65,6.5 blue
