! the roll stub: a red rod welded to the wrist link. The hand rolls on it and the jaw relay rides it
! too, so both wrist axes are bearings on one shaft and the jaw drive never crosses the roll joint.
R WS 11,0,7.5 red
C RSC D1 11,0,7.5 z -x
! the two slider rods and the brackets that guide them. A slider is what turns the corner between a
! drive that rotates about y and a joint that rotates about x.
R 9,-2,6.5 9,-2,8.5 blue
